        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Intended for use as a garment, clothing."@en , "Trousers (paijama), woven silk, gold brocade, with drawstring (ezarband), Sindh, ca. 1855; Clothing; Accessories; Textiles"@en , "Man's trousers, silk brocaded with gold-wrapped thread, in a grid pattern with repeating floral motifs. Drawstring of red silk sprang ending in a section of metal-wrapped thread with knobs of blue silk and metal-wrapped thread. Tassels, attached by loops, of metal-wrapped thread, red and blue silk thread, sequins, and red glass beads, finishing in tinsel."@en ;
